From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:46:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 213/281] Part: 2D export edge options (none, outline, all) for
 PPTX, SVG and JSON

  FreeCADCmd model.FCStd --export-pptx v.pptx --export-edges none|outline|all
  PartViews.export_pptx(objs, path, edges="outline")

Thin parts drowned in separate black edge lines and the edge lines doubled
the number of shapes in PowerPoint (28,011 shapes for 2,113 parts).

- outline: the outline of each visible face region is the line of the
  face's own freeform shape (SVG: the stroke of the face path) - no extra
  shapes.  Default for PPTX, now with 0.5 pt lines.
- all: visible edges as separate lines (as before; default for SVG/JSON).
- none: fills only (hairline in the fill colour hides the seams).

JSON leaves the edge list empty unless "all" and tells "edgeMode".
Part.projectVisible(..., edges=False) skips the edge computation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
